  "id": "premenstrual-dysphoric-disorder",
  "term": "Premenstrual Dysphoric Disorder",
  "definition": "Premenstrual dysphoric disorder is a condition marked by severe depression, irritability, and tension before menstruation, often with other physical or emotional symptoms. These symptoms are more intense and disabling than in premenstrual syndrome and usually end when, or soon after, menstruation begins.",
